      {
         "id": "c",
         "prompt": "Explain what \\( \\int_{0}^{3} \\sqrt{1 + 9x^{4}}\\,dx \\) represents in terms of the graph of \\( y = x^{3} \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\text{the length of the graph of } y = x^{3} \\text{ from } x = 0 \\text{ to } x = 3",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "For y = x^3, 1 + (dy/dx)^2 = 1 + 9x^4, so the integral is an arc length.",
